00:15:24,657 --> 00:15:28,094
Ha… if we were together, I also would’ve…

261
00:15:28,762 --> 00:15:30,630
[Sound of the seeker’s cane.]

262
00:15:31,931 --> 00:15:33,699
been taken.

263
00:15:39,472 --> 00:15:42,341
[SOHEE and EUNSEOK are located on B1.]
[Meanwhile on B1.]

264
00:15:42,609 --> 00:15:45,211
[EUNSEOK exists the kitchen.]

265
00:15:46,546 --> 00:15:49,015
[← EUNSEOK]
[SOHEE →]

266
00:15:56,289 --> 00:15:58,324
This is too much. I’m scared.

267
00:15:59,359 --> 00:16:01,961
To tell you the truth, I was really scared earlier.

268
00:16:05,331 --> 00:16:06,833
I hear something.

269
00:16:07,734 --> 00:16:10,870
[The seeker enters the basement cafeteria.]

270
00:16:11,171 --> 00:16:13,238
[The seeker →]

271
00:16:13,273 --> 00:16:15,841
[EUNSEOK →] [The seeker →] [SOHEE →]

272
00:16:19,679 --> 00:16:21,180
(Lights turned off)

273
00:16:23,083 --> 00:16:26,185
[While the seeker is searching the cafeteria, ]

274
00:16:29,022 --> 00:16:32,725
[SOHEE’s phone alarm goes off.]

275
00:16:34,127 --> 00:16:37,396
[The phone alarm breaks the silence.]

276
00:16:41,034 --> 00:16:43,603
[SOHEE ↓] [EUNSEOK ↓]
[The seeker ↑]

277
00:16:48,308 --> 00:16:54,780
[SOHEE ↓] [EUNSEOK ↓]
[The seeker ↑]

278
00:16:55,048 --> 00:16:57,550
[EUNSEOK runs to the other side.]

279
00:17:03,890 --> 00:17:06,893
[The seeker notices EUNSEOK and chases after him.]

280
00:17:12,132 --> 00:17:13,966
[EUNSEOK. I found you!]

281
00:17:21,875 --> 00:17:22,875
Ahh! That was scary.

282
00:17:23,943 --> 00:17:25,344
EUNSEOK got captured

283
00:17:25,478 --> 00:17:26,478
and I could’ve been

284
00:17:26,680 --> 00:17:27,680
captured because of my phone

285
00:17:27,914 --> 00:17:29,048
but thanks to EUNSEOK

286
00:17:29,282 --> 00:17:30,382
I didn’t get caught.

287
00:17:30,517 --> 00:17:31,517
The seeker might come here again

288
00:17:31,584 --> 00:17:32,784
because my phone alarm went off, right?

289
00:17:33,854 --> 00:17:34,854
You got captured again?

290
00:17:35,288 --> 00:17:36,756
Yea, it was scary getting caught.

291
00:17:37,056 --> 00:17:39,225
It’s really scary when you hide with the door closed.

292
00:17:39,526 --> 00:17:40,526
Yea, true.

293
00:17:40,727 --> 00:17:44,397
[Current survival rate of RIIZE is about 66.67% ]

294
00:17:44,564 --> 00:17:49,068
[SUNGCHAN, SHOTARO and the seeker are located on the 4th floor.]

295
00:17:50,837 --> 00:17:53,339
[Sound of the door opening.]

296
00:17:54,974 --> 00:17:58,277
The seeker is opening the doors.

297
00:17:59,546 --> 00:18:01,781
[Moves to another room.]

298
00:18:05,018 --> 00:18:08,187
[SHOTARO →]
[SHOTARO is hiding here.]

299
00:18:08,488 --> 00:18:09,789
The seeker is here.

300
00:18:10,456 --> 00:18:12,592
(Please, don’t come here.)

301
00:18:12,792 --> 00:18:14,393
(Please.)

302
00:18:19,732 --> 00:18:22,869
[Leaves without noticing SHOTARO.]

303
00:18:27,507 --> 00:18:29,542
[Sound of the seeker knocking on the door.]

304
00:18:29,909 --> 00:18:32,845
(The seeker is right next to me.)

305
00:18:35,348 --> 00:18:41,120
[SUNGCHAN, SHOTARO and the seeker are located on the 4th floor.]

306
00:18:41,488 --> 00:18:46,392
[The gap between them is gradually closing in.]

307
00:19:01,107 --> 00:19:03,843
[The seeker arrives in front of the room SUNGCHAN is hiding in.]

308
00:19:07,914 --> 00:19:10,983
[Sound of the seeker’s cane.]

309
00:19:12,519 --> 00:19:16,555
[The seeker searches every corner of the room.]

310
00:19:22,629 --> 00:19:23,629
[Here you are?]

311
00:19:23,696 --> 00:19:26,732
[SUNGCHAN. I found you!]
Ah! you scared me.

312
00:19:33,339 --> 00:19:35,241
Someone got captured next door.

313
00:19:39,412 --> 00:19:40,412
Phew… this is tiring.

314
00:19:42,715 --> 00:19:44,395
[← SHOTARO]
[SHOTARO’s phone alarm goes off. ]

315
00:19:46,786 --> 00:19:48,487
Hey, this is WONBIN.

316
00:19:48,488 --> 00:19:50,008
I’m in prison with EUNSEOK.

317
00:19:50,123 --> 00:19:51,524
Do you have a key?

318
00:19:51,591 --> 00:19:52,591
I do have one.

319
00:19:52,659 --> 00:19:55,094
[In the meantime, SUNGCHAN arrives in prison.]

320
00:19:55,195 --> 00:19:56,195
To avoid getting captured,

321
00:19:56,262 --> 00:19:57,782
you need to come now with the key.

322
00:19:57,931 --> 00:19:59,732
Okay, don’t call me anymore.

323
00:20:10,310 --> 00:20:13,512
[Before heading over to the prison
SHOTARO searches for the key.]

324
00:20:16,783 --> 00:20:18,217
Where is it?

325
00:20:18,718 --> 00:20:20,753
It is definitely in this room.

326
00:20:26,593 --> 00:20:27,593
Seriously, where is it?

327
00:20:28,161 --> 00:20:30,663
Come on, I searched everywhere and it’s still not here?

328
00:20:31,464 --> 00:20:35,201
[Hint for the key.]
[The laundry room on the 4th floor.]
[Rereading the hint.]

329
00:20:36,002 --> 00:20:37,870
What is this?

330
00:20:38,905 --> 00:20:39,905
[A hole in the ceiling.]

331
00:20:49,949 --> 00:20:50,749
Oh!

332
00:20:54,454 --> 00:20:55,821
I found it!

333
00:20:55,888 --> 00:20:57,857
[Found the last key.]

334
00:20:58,257 --> 00:20:59,725
I found the two keys

335
00:20:59,926 --> 00:21:01,794
I’m coming to rescue you guys.

336
00:21:03,930 --> 00:21:05,865
Hold on guys,

337
00:21:05,999 --> 00:21:09,335
I’m coming to get you out.

338
00:21:11,337 --> 00:21:13,539
Did we use up 3 keys in total so far?

339
00:21:13,840 --> 00:21:16,442
[Currently used 4 keys in total.]

340
00:21:16,510 --> 00:21:17,777
He’s here.

341
00:21:18,277 --> 00:21:20,846
[SHOTARO arrives in prison.]

342
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:22,320
You have one more key?

343
00:21:23,716 --> 00:21:26,152
Don’t save me! I’m too scared to come out.

344
00:21:26,186 --> 00:21:27,653
[3 people are locked up
and there are 2 keys.]

345
00:21:27,821 --> 00:21:31,357
I’ll save EUNSEOK and SUNGCHAN.

346
00:21:34,293 --> 00:21:38,965
[EUNSEOK and SUNGCHAN are rescued.]
SHOTARO, you rescued two people?

347
00:21:39,599 --> 00:21:41,000
I’m scared.

348
00:21:41,634 --> 00:21:43,134
[SHOTARO, EUNSEOK, SUNGCHAN and SOHEE are located on B1.]

349
00:21:43,169 --> 00:21:46,038
[Heads to the cafeteria right next to the prison.]

350
00:21:46,806 --> 00:21:49,575
SOHEE, do you have a key?

351
00:21:49,676 --> 00:21:51,544
No, I don’t!

352
00:21:52,144 --> 00:21:52,944
SOHEE doesn’t have it.

353
00:21:52,945 --> 00:21:53,445
You don’t have the key?

354
00:21:53,513 --> 00:21:54,980
We just need to stay alive for 10 minutes.

355
00:21:55,081 --> 00:21:56,282
Oh, no...

356
00:21:56,749 --> 00:22:00,319
[RIIZE used all 6 keys.]

357
00:22:00,653 --> 00:22:02,454
Is it safe to walk around together?

358
00:22:02,655 --> 00:22:04,456
Of course it’s not.

359
00:22:04,857 --> 00:22:07,393
What are they thinking? It’s not a good idea to stick together.

360
00:22:07,560 --> 00:22:08,560
What are they up to now?

361
00:22:10,129 --> 00:22:11,697
Ah... 9 minutes remaining.

362
00:22:12,231 --> 00:22:15,934
Because there are 5 people not in prison…

363
00:22:16,102 --> 00:22:17,102
we won.

364
00:22:18,771 --> 00:22:21,874
[ Timer for 20 minutes.]

365
00:22:22,175 --> 00:22:23,809
Ah… I’m locked up here for good.

366
00:22:25,945 --> 00:22:30,016
[Time’s up for 20 minutes.
WONBIN is unable to escape now.]

367
00:22:34,487 --> 00:22:35,888
It’s coming, coming, coming.

368
00:22:36,222 --> 00:22:37,356
The seeker’s coming?

369
00:22:37,556 --> 00:22:39,391
I can hear the seeker’s cane.

370
00:22:40,359 --> 00:22:42,261
[Sound of the seeker’s cane.]

371
00:22:42,762 --> 00:22:44,530
Hide over here.

372
00:22:46,499 --> 00:22:48,200
[EUNSEOK hiding behind the food storage room door.]

373
00:22:49,002 --> 00:22:52,805
[SUNGCHAN heads to the corner of the cafeteria.]

374
00:22:55,375 --> 00:22:57,776
[↑ SHOTARO] [SOHEE →]
[← EUNSEOK]
[SUNGCHAN ↓]

375
00:22:58,711 --> 00:23:02,514
[SHOTARO enters the kitchen.]

376
00:23:03,216 --> 00:23:05,785
[At the same time, the seeker enters the cafeteria.]

377
00:23:20,968 --> 00:23:21,734
[The seeker →]

378
00:23:21,834 --> 00:23:22,834
[← SUNGCHAN] [The seeker →]

379
00:23:29,375 --> 00:23:30,375
I’m sorry. I’m sorry.

380
00:23:30,609 --> 00:23:31,609
I’m sorry. I’m sorry.

381
00:23:32,278 --> 00:23:34,113
[SUNGCHAN. I found you!]

382
00:23:34,213 --> 00:23:35,614
I’m sorry. I’m sorry.

383
00:23:38,084 --> 00:23:40,452
I shouldn’t have come out.

384
00:23:40,953 --> 00:23:42,721
[Phone alarm goes off.]

385
00:23:43,657 --> 00:23:47,426
[Remaining time is 444 seconds.]

386
00:23:47,493 --> 00:23:50,463
[The seeker’s shadows, quicker than the seekers,]

387
00:23:50,763 --> 00:23:54,834
[are on their way to find you.]

388
00:24:01,640 --> 00:24:05,277
[The seeker’s shadows arrive
along with a disturbing noise.]

389
00:24:06,112 --> 00:24:07,446
Huh?

390
00:24:07,746 --> 00:24:09,114
What was that? Was that the seeker’s voice?

391
00:24:09,448 --> 00:24:10,448
What was that? What was that?

392
00:24:11,483 --> 00:24:14,786
[Sound of the shadows moving quickly.]

393
00:24:17,423 --> 00:24:21,294
The shadows are starting to move.

394
00:24:22,094 --> 00:24:26,065
[The shadows roaming around the 1st floor. ]

395
00:24:31,304 --> 00:24:32,805
(Shuts his eyes. )

396
00:24:35,741 --> 00:24:39,812
[Enters the room where ANTON is in.]

397
00:24:41,547 --> 00:24:43,215
[Closely approaches ANTON. ]

398
00:24:49,722 --> 00:24:51,824
[Leaves without noticing him.]

399
00:24:54,760 --> 00:24:57,196
[With no luck, moves on to the next room.]

400
00:24:57,529 --> 00:24:58,797
[ANTON sniffs his nose.]

401
00:25:01,033 --> 00:25:02,401
I want to go home.

402
00:25:05,104 --> 00:25:07,840
[SHOTARO, EUNSEOK, the seeker and SOHEE are located on B1.]

403
00:25:08,374 --> 00:25:09,674
[The shadows go downstairs to the basement cafeteria.]

404
00:25:10,309 --> 00:25:12,645
It’s here. It’s here. It’s here. It’s here.

405
00:25:16,615 --> 00:25:18,917
[The roaring of the shadows.]

406
00:25:19,218 --> 00:25:22,221
[Discovers SOHEE who was hiding.]

407
00:25:24,724 --> 00:25:26,091
[SOHEE →]

408
00:25:26,592 --> 00:25:28,861
[The shadows surround SOHEE.]

409
00:25:29,261 --> 00:25:31,463
[Loudly summon the other seekers.]

410
00:25:33,499 --> 00:25:35,034
[SOHEE quickly escapes.]

411
00:25:36,735 --> 00:25:38,804
[The seeker immediately approaches.]

412
00:25:44,076 --> 00:25:45,076
[SOHEE screaming.]

413
00:25:48,047 --> 00:25:48,847
[The seeker ↓]

414
00:25:48,914 --> 00:25:49,654
[The seeker ↓] [SOHEE ↓]

415
00:25:49,715 --> 00:25:51,283
[Eventually, they run into each other.]

416
00:25:51,984 --> 00:25:53,652
[SOHEE. I found you!]

417
00:26:01,260 --> 00:26:05,297
But, we can’t save him because we ran out of keys...

418
00:26:05,764 --> 00:26:06,764
[Current survival rate is 50%.]

419
00:26:07,433 --> 00:26:09,568
[EUNSEOK →]
[EUNSEOK hiding in the food storage room.]

420
00:26:10,736 --> 00:26:12,871
[The sound of the shadows getting closer.]

421
00:26:20,513 --> 00:26:23,582
[The seeker and the shadow
both enter the food storage room.]

422
00:26:32,992 --> 00:26:36,061
[Finds EUNSEOK behind the door]

423
00:26:36,261 --> 00:26:39,531
[but just leaves.]

424
00:26:40,266 --> 00:26:41,266
[EUNSEOK laughing.]

425
00:26:42,201 --> 00:26:43,569
Why are they just leaving?

426
00:26:44,736 --> 00:26:45,736
[There’s no way for them to just pass by.]

427
00:26:48,841 --> 00:26:50,741
[EUNSEOK. I found you!]

428
00:26:55,714 --> 00:26:57,983
[Current survival rate is 33.33%.]

429
00:26:58,250 --> 00:26:59,050
Hey, call everyone!

430
00:26:59,051 --> 00:27:00,051
Call SHOTARO.

431
00:27:00,119 --> 00:27:01,459
SHOTARO doesn’t have the keys either.

432
00:27:01,553 --> 00:27:03,855
Or call ANTON.

433
00:27:04,123 --> 00:27:05,483
[The remaining time left for hide-and-seek is 100 seconds.]

434
00:27:05,658 --> 00:27:07,860
I think it’s obvious that we lost the game.

435
00:27:08,627 --> 00:27:10,796
[There’s no other method to increase the survival rate.]

436
00:27:16,535 --> 00:27:18,904
It’s over?

437
00:27:20,072 --> 00:27:22,207
Why did you get captured?

438
00:27:22,474 --> 00:27:23,608
Did we lose the game?

439
00:27:23,876 --> 00:27:25,556
We lost. More than 50% of the people are locked in here.

440
00:27:25,778 --> 00:27:27,813
[Come out, come out wherever you are!]

441
00:27:33,452 --> 00:27:35,854
[End of hide-and-seek.]

442
00:27:37,189 --> 00:27:38,991
Is it over? Is it really over?

443
00:27:41,360 --> 00:27:44,663
[ANTON finally comes out from the hiding spot.]

444
00:27:46,031 --> 00:27:49,868
[Heads over to meet the rest of the members.]

445
00:27:52,838 --> 00:27:54,673
[SHOTARO heads over to the prison.]

446
00:27:54,673 --> 00:27:55,973
It’s over. It’s really over.

447
00:27:56,008 --> 00:27:56,708
It’s over. It’s over.

448
00:27:56,775 --> 00:27:57,842
We lost.

449
00:27:57,876 --> 00:27:59,745
We lost because WONBIN didn’t come out of the prison.

450
00:28:00,045 --> 00:28:02,748
But honestly what was ANTON doing this whole time?

451
00:28:03,515 --> 00:28:06,317
[The youngest disappeared right when the game started.]
He never came out during the game.

452
00:28:06,352 --> 00:28:07,686
I never saw him once.

453
00:28:07,953 --> 00:28:09,354
Wow, ANTON is a true legend.

454
00:28:10,422 --> 00:28:12,825
[ANTON finally appears.]
Hey ANTON, what were you doing?

455
00:28:12,958 --> 00:28:14,226
ANTON, you never came out?

456
00:28:16,862 --> 00:28:18,964
Looking at your hair, I guess you never did.

457
00:28:19,031 --> 00:28:20,065
You were sleeping right?

458
00:28:20,265 --> 00:28:21,365
In fact, I even called him

459
00:28:21,867 --> 00:28:22,940
and he didn't say a word!

460
00:28:23,068 --> 00:28:23,668
I know!

461
00:28:23,735 --> 00:28:26,671
You did call me but the seeker was right outside.

462
00:28:26,905 --> 00:28:28,185
I thought we would definitely win because

463
00:28:28,407 --> 00:28:30,409
SHOTARO saved 2 people.

464
00:28:30,709 --> 00:28:32,277
I thought I would never get caught but

465
00:28:32,544 --> 00:28:34,579
the shadow flipped the chair.

466
00:28:34,780 --> 00:28:36,248
(I screamed like this.)

467
00:28:39,518 --> 00:28:41,019
I quickly escaped

468
00:28:41,153 --> 00:28:42,286
and ran up the stairs to get away

469
00:28:42,721 --> 00:28:44,456
but the seeker was coming towards me like this from upstairs.

470
00:28:46,558 --> 00:28:48,493
[Phone alarm goes off.]
Oh, a message came.

471
00:28:49,194 --> 00:28:57,569
[Because the survival rate was less than 50%,
the chance to present BRIIZE with some treats is now gone.]

472
00:28:58,170 --> 00:29:00,639
I had no courage to save anyone.

473
00:29:00,773 --> 00:29:02,293
It’s fine. It was really scary anyway.

474
00:29:05,010 --> 00:29:07,646
[The seeker’s terrifying scream.]

475
00:29:10,482 --> 00:29:11,883
- Hold on!
- That scared me!

476
00:29:12,117 --> 00:29:13,552
[One more round?]

477
00:29:16,054 --> 00:29:18,924
[SUMBAKKOKJIL]
